{"id": "EUVD-2026-102267", "enisaUuid": "b6585927-0dc5-3a50-89ff-168b98e09424", "description": "libregf through 20260526 contains a heap out-of-bounds read in libregf_value_item_read_value_data() because it bounds value data size without subtracting the 4-byte old-format cell offset. Attackers can supply a crafted version 1.0/1.1 REGF hive with a value data cell ending its hive bin to leak adjacent heap bytes or crash parsers like regfexport and plaso.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:32", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T01:19:40", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/libregf-value-data-offset-oob-read", "https://github.com/libyal/libregf/blob/1a4bd856484263caa4a5e0d6ba377c3dc69150c7/libregf/libregf_value_item.c#L789-L935", "https://github.com/libyal/libregf", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libregf-through-20260526-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-libregf-value-item-read-value-data"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111140", "GHSA-4g68-6f29-pjf8"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "c0f3c63f-44b2-342b-9254-7a67ff75097e", "product": {"name": "libregf", "vendor": {"name": "libyal"}}, "product_version": "0 \u226420260526"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0e40c835-f86b-3cc4-b509-a465282cbe00", "vendor": {"name": "libyal"}}], "isExploited": false}